          "id": "9ceacf69-0e50-48b7-bb3c-428cbf89e24a",
          "memory": "Alex bought a tiny basil plant with only three fingernail-sized leaves in a thimble/shot-glass-sized pot for $3.50 from the little nursery by the grocery store on September 20, 2026, after stopping just to look. He confirmed it smells like basil after rubbing one leaf, and the cashier said \"good luck with that one.\"",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "aae80bae-fc3b-42b8-ab7b-4aadc4c4225e",
          "memory": "Alex placed his tiny three-leaf basil on his windowsill next to his existing succulent, where it is dwarfed by a mug, house keys and key fob, and a coffee spoon bigger than its pot. He watered it with a tablespoon and nearly drowned it, gives it 50/50 survival odds due to weird sun, plans to repot if it survives the week, and joked he will make pesto in about 10 years.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "efaabea2-825c-41c0-aeab-4ecf59bb2408",
          "memory": "Alex's mom keeps telling him to get more green stuff in his apartment, and Alex said she would laugh if she saw his tiny basil plant, with User suggesting he send her the keys-comparison photo. Alex counts the tiny amount of green as one plant.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "69d0d9b2-1c6a-4daa-a0a0-8affca280952",
          "memory": "On September 20, 2026, User spent Sunday doing laundry hell with the washer running and dryer beeping, saying the couch was covered in laundry so they were camped on the floor while chatting with Alex.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "66c88d49-8d8c-44bd-92f9-1a2259f11555",
          "memory": "On September 20, 2026, User caught the second half of a game and discussed a wild 4th-quarter call with Alex, who said he yelled at the call and scared his new tiny basil plant.",
